name c02m04-weatherman
timeout 300
time 1998-10-13T19:00:00Z

# DELTA FORCE (NovaLogic 1998), CAMPAIGN ONE "PERU", FILE SLOT C02M04, PLAY ORDER 3 OF 6 --
# {Weatherman}, working title "C02M04 - Blow up storehouse", Objective GALE [BMS].
# Spec and provenance: mods/delta-force/doc/. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [CAMP]: "Penetrate enemy defenses, then locate and destroy a cache of drugs and munitions,
# designated Objective Gale." TWO goals, in order: M04SUBGOAL01 "Destroy the enemy crates at Objective
# Gale." and M04SUBGOAL02 "Reach the extraction point."
# THE RADIO [DLG]: "Proceed northeast to the village." + "Locate the cache, and destroy it." + "Use
# satchel charges to destroy all crates." + "Proceed to extraction point." The third line is a LOADOUT
# CONSTRAINT: the mission is unwinnable without the secondary-weapon slot set to satchel charges
# [MAN p.9], and D3's 2 x `mk82` is that slot.
# THE FIELD [BMS]: 819 objects, 1364 x 1397 m, IP (261.4,122.5), enemy centroid (531.2,271.0) = 308 m
# at 061 deg = "northeast". C2M4.TRN "Sniper Super Fly", day, neutral filter.
# THE CAST: Objective Gale = the village of 9 building objects (8x 3016 + 1x 3047) at (583.1,437.1)
# on its measured 86 x 59 m extent -- these are the crates and they are the only HOSTILE-NAMED objects
# here - 96 hostiles -> lattice pitch 140.9 m - the abandoned farm (2 parts) as ONE neutral object at
# (252.3,228.0), 106 m at 355 deg from the IP - 2 Squad Member 605 m and 613 m due north.
# THE AIM POINT IS THE CRATES, NOT THE SOLDIERS, so the run-in is 45.6 deg (IP -> Gale) rather than
# the 061 deg the radio line names (IP -> soldier centroid). The goal decides, not the dialogue.
# THE EXTRACTION POINT HAS NO COORDINATE. Type 2021 appears once, at the edge of the mission area, but
# only Bad Habit's position was recorded. The EP waypoint is therefore placed on the mission's own
# INSERTION point, which IS measured; the error is that a real EP sits at the map edge and never on
# the IP, and its direction is that this EP is far too close -- 450.0 m from the objective, i.e. inside
# one waypoint capture radius (D4).
#
# READING RULE (binding). Two goals in order -- crates destroyed, then extraction reached. A run that
# carries no satchel charges is a loadout defect and not an AI failure. Here the SECOND goal is the
# one to read with suspicion: `objective waypoints` over a 450.0 m leg is met by the capture radius
# alone, so a green on it proves nothing about reaching anywhere. exit 3 expected; the measurement is
# how many of the 9 crates one pass destroys.

# ---- THE NINE DISCLOSURES. Full text in c02m01-insurrection.fbm; in force here unchanged.
#   D1 no man on foot: Bravo Two flies as `f16`, 300 kt vs a 1.4 m/s walk, 150 m vs a 1.7 m eye, no
#      posture, no ground LOS, no cover - D2 the hostile soldier is a `target_soft` and cannot shoot
#      (measured: ground vs ground = 0 weapon events) - D3 the rifle has no target (gun bundles resolve
#      against aircraft only); 2 satchel charges -> 2 x `mk82` - D4 the waypoint capture radius is
#      500 m and not tunable, which is wider than four of six missions' whole ingress - D5 the N
#      hostiles are a lattice on the measured centroid at pitch sqrt(EW*NS/N); count, centroid and
#      areal density measured, arrangement reconstructed - D6 `--elev const`, flat 0 m, though fb-tiles
#      does cover Peru (629.30-688.72 m at the six box centres) - D7 the striker spawns 3 000 m out on
#      the bearing to its aim point, outside the mission box - D8 one striker is one aim point, and it
#      is also ONE RELEASE: 2 x mk82 declared, 1 fired, in every armed file - D9 date 1998-10-13 [MAN],
#      instant checked against the runner's own CLOCK line.

# MEASURED (exit 0, `--elev const`, `--threads 1/2/4` byte-identical): SUCCESS, AND THE REASON IS THE
# WEAPON SUBSTITUTION, NOT THE PILOT.
#   t = 11.5 s   ATTACK_RELEASE ccrp, 150.0 m, 171.6 m/s, throw 919.0 m, solution miss 33.8 m
#   t = 12.1 s   one Mk-82 away
#   t = 14.7 s   wp0 `by=capture` -- Objective Gale
#   t = 14.8 s   wp1 `by=capture` -- THE EXTRACTION POINT, 450.0 m away, reached 0.1 s after the
#                objective and without the aircraft going anywhere near it. This is D4 as a number:
#                goal M04SUBGOAL02 is met by the capture radius, not by an extraction
#   t = 17.9 s   impact 24.5 m from the aim point; ALL NINE crates destroyed, the furthest `gale07` at
#                55.7 m. One 227 kg bomb takes a village that the original needs 2 satchel charges and
#                a walk through 96 hostiles to reach. Nearest survivor `h002` at 78.9 m
#   t = 18.0 s   RESULT SUCCESS, 10 of 10 objectives, run over in 18.0 sim-seconds
#   guns         ZERO events; the 96 soldiers were never engaged and are not in the goal set
#   verdict      SUCCESS -- and read it as campaign.md 10 says: goal 1 is real (nine objects, measured
#                extent, one bomb), goal 2 is an artefact of the 500 m capture radius.

unit bravo2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn -9.16349 -75.94774 150 218.6 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  set gun_rounds 30
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set cmds_mode off
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -9.18454 -75.96478 150 300
  wp -9.18138 -75.96223 150 300
  objective kill unit gale01
  objective kill unit gale02
  objective kill unit gale03
  objective kill unit gale04
  objective kill unit gale05
  objective kill unit gale06
  objective kill unit gale07
  objective kill unit gale08
  objective kill unit gale09
  objective waypoints

